 "reportTemplate": {
  "summary": "Dashboard was already in edit mode with the top bar showing time range \"Last 6 hours\" and auto-refresh \"1m\" (button aria-label \"current interval 1 minute selected\"), both confirmed by reading the toolbar, so no time-picker changes were needed. I clicked Save dashboard and ticked \"Update default refresh value\" — the only checkbox the drawer contained — which enabled the previously-disabled Save button; clicking Save produced the \"Dashboard saved\" alert, and \"Exit edit\" removed the edit-mode toolbar (now only Mark as favorite / Share / Edit). One deviation to flag: the drawer had no \"Update default time range\" checkbox to tick, because Grafana renders it only when the current range differs from the saved default and that 6-hour default was already persisted in the previous save this session. That default is verified present rather than assumed: reloading the dashboard with no query parameters still shows \"Last 6 hours\" with refresh \"1m\" in the top bar, alongside both panels (\"{{v2}} Notes\" displaying \"Notes for run {{v2}}\" and \"{{v2}} Availability\"). So the save succeeded and both requested defaults are persisted; ticked = \"Update default refresh value\" only.",
